<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bank of England</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1694</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bank of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> was founded in 1694 to lend money to the English government, primarily to finance war against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. It managed government debt and became the central bank of the United Kingdom. Its creation allowed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> to borrow on a large scale, which is seen as a key foundation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a>'s military and commercial power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bank-of-england.jpg" alt="Bank of England" width="320" height="250" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: acediscovery · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bank-of-England.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
